.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-server-storage-mount-list - List object storage mounts of a server


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro server storage-mount list  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List object storage mounts of a server

.PP
Mount a bucket of your Gyro Object Storage service on a Linux server (systemd) as a folder (rclone FUSE mount with a local write cache, starts on boot, reconnects). Each mount gets its own access key limited to that one bucket (read-only or read/write); it does not use your key limit and is deleted with the mount. Gyro Cloud Istanbul (tr-ist-1) servers apply it automatically (\fBautomatic: true\fR); other servers run \fBinstall_command\fR once. Free; S3 traffic counts towards the storage service. Protected Storage buckets: read-only by default (2.20.0). Supported servers: Gyro Cloud (Istanbul and EU), Turkey VDS, dedicated servers.

.PP
API: GET /cloud/servers/{id}/storage-mounts (operationId listStorageMounts, scope cloud_read)


